    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="1121" n="1081" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1081"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">683.84A/12–1852: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 533<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Israel (Davis) to the
                        Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d533-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tel
                                Aviv</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-12-18T20:00:00+02:00">December 18, 1952—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>994. Embtel 902<anchor n="2" xml:id="d533-f2"/> and Damascus Embtel 411 to
                        Dept.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d533-f3"/> FonMin Sharett confirmed to me today
                    Israel interest in continuing conversations with Syria. He stated “matter by no
                    means dormant” but on contrary subj active consideration. He reminded me that
                    there had been important change in high level milit command namely appointment
                    Makleff to succeed Yadin as Chief of Staff but stated he understood new milit
                    auths now ready with recommendations which he expects to receive Cabinet
                    consideration within next few days. He stated also that IG wld not have
                    postponed resumption of conversations to await outcome of GA action on
                    eight-power res if long delay wld have been involved, but since only few days’
                    delay in question he had thought it advisable await outcome before arranging
                    definite date for continuation talks with Syria.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d533-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d533-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to New York, Damascus, Beirut, Amman, Baghdad, Cairo, London, and Paris;
                    sent by pouch to Ankara, Jidda, and Jerusalem.</p>
